            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary steal syndrome following internal mammary artery bypass surgery: incidence and recommendations for avoiding it].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>318-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With the increased use of the internal mammary artery for coronary artery bypass surgery, new complications are seen. This report describes the twelfth case of a coronary-subclavian steal syndrome. It summarizes all previously reported cases and makes some recommendations in order to avoid and treat this condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
